<p>On July 2, during the city's Rodeo Days celebration, Cloverdale Foods Company set a record for the "World's Longest Hot Dog" under the supervision of Guinness World Records staff. The previous record, set in Pennsylvania, was 15 feet 3 inches. A team of 30 Cloverdale employees constructed a hot dog measuring 21 feet 4.25 inches. The record stood for six years, until a team in Monterrey, Mexico, produced a 375-foot hot dog on September 27, 2008.</p>

<h3>2003</h3>

